This project's data model was informed by reading these MIT-licensed projects.
No code was copied from any of them; the debts are conceptual and are recorded
here so they are not mistaken for original invention:

- brianraines/job-hunt (MIT) — https://github.com/brianraines/job-hunt
  Borrowed ideas: directive files as the operator's stated intent; a committed
  "seen" set so a posting is only resurfaced when it materially changes;
  one dated evaluation report per company rather than a mutable record; the
  refuse-to-write-unless-git-ignores-it safeguard on private data; recording
  the applicant tracking system host per company instead of an aggregator URL.

- Remotivated/job-hunt-skills (MIT) — https://github.com/Remotivated/job-hunt-skills
  Borrowed ideas: a canonical-facts file that generated materials are checked
  against; separating a source-of-truth career record from per-role tailored
  derivatives; markdown-first authoring with rendering as a separate step.

- Gensoo/JobHuntAgent (MIT) — https://github.com/Gensoo/JobHuntAgent
  Borrowed ideas: fit scoring as a first-class artifact of the pipeline.

